sections.s2_technical:
The teeing collector accepts three arguments. The first downstream collector processes each element independently. The second downstream collector also processes each element independently. Both run in parallel on the same stream — every element passes through BOTH collectors. When all elements are consumed, the merger BiFunction receives the results of both collectors and combines them into the final output.

```java
// MIN and MAX salary in ONE pass:
record SalaryRange(Optional<BigDecimal> min, Optional<BigDecimal> max) {}

SalaryRange range = employees.stream()
    .map(Employee::getSalary)
    .collect(Collectors.teeing(
        Collectors.minBy(Comparator.naturalOrder()),    // downstream 1: find min
        Collectors.maxBy(Comparator.naturalOrder()),    // downstream 2: find max
        SalaryRange::new));                              // merger: combine results
// SalaryRange{min=Optional[900000], max=Optional[1800000]}
```

Without teeing, you need two separate stream operations:

```java
// (Avoid) TWO PASSES — less efficient:
Optional<BigDecimal> min = employees.stream().map(Employee::getSalary)
    .min(Comparator.naturalOrder());   // pass 1
Optional<BigDecimal> max = employees.stream().map(Employee::getSalary)
    .max(Comparator.naturalOrder());   // pass 2
// Two iterations over the same data!

// (Recommended) ONE PASS with teeing:
// Both min and max computed simultaneously — half the iteration work.
```

Teeing can combine ANY two collectors. Count and sum:

```java
record CountAndSum(long count, BigDecimal sum) {}

CountAndSum result = trades.stream()
    .map(Trade::getAmount)
    .collect(Collectors.teeing(
        Collectors.counting(),                              // downstream 1
        Collectors.reducing(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add),  // downstream 2
        CountAndSum::new));
// CountAndSum{count=6, sum=1185737}
```

Teeing with groupingBy-style results:

```java
// Settled count AND total amount in one pass:
record SettlementSummary(long settledCount, BigDecimal totalAmount) {}

SettlementSummary summary = trades.stream()
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)
    .collect(Collectors.teeing(
        Collectors.counting(),
        Collectors.mapping(Trade::getAmount,
            Collectors.reducing(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add)),
        SettlementSummary::new));
```

Teeing with partitioned results:

```java
// Average of values BELOW and ABOVE a threshold:
record ThresholdAnalysis(double belowAvg, double aboveAvg) {}

ThresholdAnalysis analysis = amounts.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.teeing(
        Collectors.filtering(a -> a.compareTo(threshold) < 0,
            Collectors.averagingDouble(BigDecimal::doubleValue)),
        Collectors.filtering(a -> a.compareTo(threshold) >= 0,
            Collectors.averagingDouble(BigDecimal::doubleValue)),
        ThresholdAnalysis::new));
```

